    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Auto-post RSS feed items to Bluesky and Mastodon\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Runs automatically every hour.\n2. Fetches the latest items from the RSS feed.\n3. Publishes posts to Bluesky and Mastodon via the SocialRobot API.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Install the SocialRobot community node and connect your SocialRobot API credential (API key: socialrobot.io, Scheduler -> API Keys).\n- [ ] Set the RSS feed URL to your own feed.\n- [ ] Select your connected SocialRobot account in each Publish node.\n\n### Customization\n\nPoint the RSS node at a different feed to reuse the workflow for another blog or channel. Remove the Publish nodes you do not need to target fewer platforms. Adjust the trigger interval to control exactly how often the workflow runs. The RSS node can point at any feed, so the workflow adapts to a new source in seconds.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 586
      },
